bo2mp: notices for third-party material

================================================================================
Fonts built into the binary
================================================================================

The two fonts listed here are embedded with `include_bytes!`, so every bo2mp
build carries them, and any archive containing a bo2mp binary must carry their
licence texts too.

1. Oxanium, file crates/ui/assets/Oxanium-Regular.ttf, source https://github.com/sevmeyer/oxanium
   Oxanium notice: Copyright 2019 The Oxanium Project Authors
   Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (whole text: crates/ui/assets/OFL-Oxanium.txt)

2. GNU FreeFont, file crates/console/assets/FreeMono.otf, source https://www.gnu.org/software/freefont/
   FreeFont notice: Copyright (C) 2002-2012 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
   Licence: GNU GPL version 3 or later plus the GNU font exception (whole text:
   crates/console/assets/COPYING-FreeFont.txt). Thanks to that exception, a
   program or document that only uses the font is not itself put under the GPL,
   which is what allows embedding it in a bo2mp binary. The font file is
   unchanged and stays under the GPL.

================================================================================
Copied third-party code and data
================================================================================

1. Portal Gun model and texture, in crates/asset_source/src/portalgun.rs
   Taken from MeowMC's Portal Gun mod (repository https://github.com/iPortalTeam/PortalGun),
   converted from portalgun.geo.json and portalgun.png into cube and pixel tables.
   Portal Gun notice: Copyright (c) 2021 MeowMC
   Licence: MIT (whole text: crates/asset_source/src/LICENSE-portalgun-MIT.txt)

2. wgpu-hal 29.0.4, in third_party/wgpu-hal, from https://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu
   wgpu-hal notice: Copyright (c) 2025 The gfx-rs developers
   Licence: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (whole texts: third_party/wgpu-hal/LICENSE.MIT, third_party/wgpu-hal/LICENSE.APACHE)
   Local change: src/vulkan/swapchain/native.rs (look for "bo2mp patch") waits
   again for a swap-chain image that is slow, rather than losing the device.

The crates that bo2mp depends on are the ones Cargo.toml declares, each under its
own licence.

